man dotfiles

add descriptions to neovim binds
ensure all shadows neovim binds get alt bind, e.g., i_CTRL-K

neovim bind ideas

ctrl-enter -> open action menu, e.g., like ctrl-enter in opencode
<Leader><Leader> as a "ctrl-shift" kind of overload for less common actions

neovim keys to consider remapping

s - Flash; default `s` is redundant with `cl`; restore default `S`

Z - backspace in normal mode - almost always use something else to delete stuff in normal mode

H & L - top / bottom of screen - rarely useful, prime home row keys

X - exchange operator; default delete backward is redundant with `dh`

C & D - change/delete to end of line are redundant with `c$`/`d$`, but convenient

`-` - previous line at first nonblank is rarely useful

~ - single-character case toggle is less useful than the `g~` operator

| - exact-column motion is mainly useful in macros and fixed-width text

: - will remap to register-replace

m & M - will remap to "move"

ctrl-space in insert mode

- need to find an alt bind for setting marks

neovim stuff

- crtl-h needs to be <BS> in picker / fzf
- plugin to run rg on project and show hits in quickfix
- project wide find/replace (or on all open files, or folder).
- nvim cannot have any alt binds. snacks explorer has them by default but they need to be remapped. will need to check any plugins for alt binds and remap

# mini.nvim

* = done and fully setup
+ = added and partially setup
y = yes, will use
n = no can't or won't use

- [*] mini.ai            Extend and create a/i textobjects
- [n] mini.align         Align text interactively
  - [*] => not useful enough to justify a mapping
- [*] mini.comment       Comment lines
- [+] mini.completion    Completion and signature help
- [*] mini.keymap        Special key mappings
- [*] mini.move          Move any selection in any direction
- [n] mini.operators     Text edit operators
  - [*] => use substitute.nvim exchange and native operators
- [*] mini.pairs         Autopairs
- [y] mini.snippets      Manage and expand snippets
- [n] mini.splitjoin     Split and join arguments
  - [*] => use Wansmer/treesj with `gS`
- [*] mini.surround      Surround actions
- [*] mini.basics        Common configuration presets
- [*] mini.bracketed     Go forward/backward with square brackets
- [*] mini.bufremove     Remove buffers
- [n] mini.clue          Show next key clues
  - [*] => use folke/which-key.nvim
- [*] mini.cmdline       Command line tweaks
- [n] mini.deps          Plugin manager
  - [*] => use folke/lazy.nvim
- [n] mini.diff          Work with diff hunks
  - [*] => use lewis6991/gitsigns.nvim
- [*] mini.extra         Extra ‘mini.nvim’ functionality
- [n] mini.files         Navigate and manipulate file system
